5. RESTRUCTURE THE CODEBASE SAFELY
==================================================

After the audit, propose a clean production-oriented repository structure.

The structure should:

- Separate frontend concerns from backend concerns
- Separate API routes/controllers from business logic
- Separate business logic from infrastructure
- Separate database access from application services
- Centralize configuration
- Centralize environment validation
- Separate reusable libraries/services
- Make testing easier
- Make deployment easier
- Make future microservices possible without prematurely converting everything into microservices
- Avoid circular dependencies
- Avoid duplicated business logic
- Avoid duplicated API implementations
- Avoid legacy/dead code
- Make ownership boundaries obvious

Do NOT over-engineer the MVP.

Use a modular monolith architecture where appropriate.

The architecture should be capable of evolving into:

Modular Monolith
        ↓
Service Extraction
        ↓
Selective Microservices

without requiring a complete rewrite.

